# A disk that cannot be mounted: the service dies each time. `init` sees it and
# restarts three times, and then the shell runs without a volume.
! panicked
< fsd: mount:
< init: storage failed
< fsd: mount:
< init: storage failed
< fsd: mount:
< init: storage failed
< fsd: mount:
< init: storage failed
< init: no more restarts
x init: storage failed
< zosh$ 
> ls\r
< zosh: no volume
< zosh$ 
> poweroff\r
